3513e1032" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436813 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436806 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436813 1069 "q-130841" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436813 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436813 1071 "Let  $E=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436813 1072 #uuid "0469c521-df52-516d-97d5-643098592b19" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436813 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $-15$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-15{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}$ to $A.$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436814 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436809 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436814 1069 "q-130863" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436814 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436814 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436814 1072 #uuid "338846a1-5093-5e28-a69f-a5c5dede7770" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436814 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}=7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436815 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436810 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436815 1069 "q-75075" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436815 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436815 1071 "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436815 1072 #uuid "45f3ee1a-e687-51c7-8953-3c231936ec3d" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436815 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-8$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-8){R}_{1}$ to $A.$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436816 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436808 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436816 1069 "q-42809" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436816 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436816 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436816 1072 #uuid "4e584c32-a3dd-5eaa-a4dc-b23f04848d16" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436816 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436817 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436812 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436817 1069 "q-31977" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436817 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436817 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436817 1072 #uuid "535f214d-c021-5eea-9acd-b13d4504df24" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436817 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row  operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436818 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436805 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436818 1069 "q-75085" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436818 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436818 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix  multiplication." 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436818 1072 #uuid "83a65485-4098-56b8-8fd5-9fb601be0cb0" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436818 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436819 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436803 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436819 1069 "q-130842" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436819 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436819 1071 "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436819 1072 #uuid "88681796-21e9-5e72-a195-e1da66276721" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436819 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-6$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1}$ to $A.$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436820 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436804 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436820 1069 "q-42759" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436820 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436820 1071 "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436820 1072 #uuid "b4493b8f-a3b6-5d7e-9641-4ac3f05dd564" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436820 1074 "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of the identity matrix and adding $5$ times the second row: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}$ to $A.$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436821 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436807 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436821 1069 "q-75088" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436821 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436821 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}\\,$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436821 1072 #uuid "cc406c3a-4f36-5f35-99c4-51a064b8434e" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436821 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}$  to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436822 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436811 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436822 1069 "q-75087" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436822 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436822 1071 "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436822 1072 #uuid "f990568f-351a-543d-9726-4bfca20a8616" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true] [17592186436822 1074 "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$  \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" 13194139534809 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-041b2509-a556-5b7c-ab45-9ca5fd9c3cc1" 17592186436753 "answer-06e05fbe-65fb-57d3-abc5-dad8fbda182c" 17592186436754 "answer-07e35b25-669e-55d1-afe7-e324171bb24a" 17592186436755 "answer-08df48ed-79af-5bf2-85ef-d1439433ab47" 17592186436756 "answer-08e24a6d-b6f5-53e0-a5c7-349a536